un cas est une fraude. Ensuite, dites-moi quoi faire.","Tarjeta bloqueada
",visa,"Pour r	soudre le blocage de votre carte, vous devez contacter directement votre banque 	mettrice. Bien que Visa fournisse l'infrastructure, c'est votre 	tablissement financier qui d	cide de bloquer une transaction et qui dispose des d	tails sp	cifiques sur le motif du d	clin. Pour obtenir une assistance imm	diate : 1. Appelez le num	ro au dos de votre carte Visa. 2. Si vous n'avez pas accs ␀ ce num	ro, vous pouvez contacter les Services mondiaux d'assistance clientle de Visa (GCAS) 24h/24 au +1 303 967 1090 (ou au 0800 1 8397 depuis la France). Concernant votre demande sur les rgles de fraude, Visa ne divulgue pas les d	tails techniques et propri	taires de sa logique de s	curit	 afin de maintenir l'int	grit	 du r	seau et de prot	ger les porteurs de carte contre les tentatives de fraude r	elles.",Fraud and Travel Support,replied,product_issue,The issuer/bank is responsible for specific decline reasons and unblocking cards (data/visa/support.md). Visa omits proprietary security logic from documentation to protect the network (data/visa/support/consumer/visa-rules.md). GCAS contact information and emergency support procedures are documented in data/visa/support/consumer/travel-support.md.
I am facing multiple issues in my project. all requests to claude with aws bedrock is failing,Issues in Project,claude,"I'm sorry to hear you're experiencing failures with Claude on Amazon Bedrock. To troubleshoot this issue, please verify the following:

1. **Credentials:** Confirm your AWS credentials are loading correctly by running `aws sts get-caller-identity` in your terminal.
2. **Region:** Ensure your `AWS_REGION` environment variable is set to a region where the specific Claude model you are using is enabled.
3. **Model Access:** Verify that you have requested and been granted access to the Claude models within the Amazon Bedrock console.

Since Claude on Amazon Bedrock is a managed AWS service, for further technical assistance or if the issues persist, please contact AWS Support directly or reach out to your AWS account manager. You can also visit AWS re:Post for community support.",Amazon Bedrock Integration,replied,product_issue,Troubleshooting steps for credentials and regions are cited from data/claude/claude-code/launch-guides/14552646-troubleshoot-claude-code-installation-and-authentication.md. The policy to contact AWS Support for Bedrock-related issues is cited from data/claude/amazon-bedrock/7996921-i-use-claude-in-amazon-bedrock-who-do-i-contact-for-customer-support-inquiries.md. Guidance on model access is from data/claude/amazon-bedrock/7996920-how-do-i-get-access-to-claude-in-amazon-bedrock.md.
one of my employee has left. I want to remove them from our hackerrank hiring account,Employee leaving the company,hackerrank,"To remove an employee from your HackerRank hiring account, you can either deactivate them globally or remove them from their assigned teams. Please note that you must have Company Admin or Team Admin permissions to perform these actions.

### Deactivating a User
1. Locate the user in your **User Management** or **Teams Management** list.
2. Click the **ellipsis (⋯)** icon next to the user’s name.
3. Select **Deactivate User** and confirm in the dialog box.

### Removing a Team Member
1. Log in to your **HackerRank for Work** account.
2. Click your profile icon and select **Teams Management**.
3. Go to the **Teams** tab and select the specific team the employee belongs to.
4. Under the **Users** tab, click the **delete (trash can)** icon in the **Action** column next to the user's name.

Note: If a user belongs to only one team, removing them from that team will effectively lock their access to the platform. If your organization uses SCIM (e.g., Okta), you should deprovision them through your identity provider or click the **X** icon in the SCIM user list to transfer their resources to the Company Owner automatically.",User Management,replied,product_issue,Deactivation steps are found in data/hackerrank/skillup/getting-started/3868789028-user-management.md. Team removal steps are cited from data/hackerrank/settings/teams-management/2203617737-manage-team-members.md. SCIM and resource transfer details are from data/hackerrank/integrations/single-sign-on-sso/3939437783-setting-up-scim-provisioning-with-okta.md.
i am a professor in a college and wanted to setup a claude lti key for my students,Claude for students,claude,"Setting up the Claude LTI integration requires a Claude for Education plan and administrator access to your Learning Management System (LMS), such as Canvas. If you are not a system administrator, you will need to coordinate with your IT department to complete the following steps: 1. Create a Developer Key: In Canvas, navigate to Admin > Developer Keys and create a new LTI Key using Redirect URI 'https://claude.ai/lti/launch', OIDC Initiation URL 'https://claude.ai/api/lti/login', and JWK method 'https://claude.ai/api/lti/keys'. 2. Install the App: In Canvas Admin > Settings > Apps, select 'By Client ID' and enter the ID generated from the developer key. 3. Enable Connector in Claude: Sign into your Claude for Education admin console, navigate to Organization settings > Connectors, and enable Canvas by providing your domain, Client ID, and Deployment ID. For more detailed instructions, please consult your university's administrator or the official Claude documentation.",Claude for Education,replied,product_issue,Integration steps and administrator requirements are detailed in data/claude/claude-for-education/11725453-set-up-the-claude-lti-in-canvas-by-instructure.md (https://support.claude.com/en/articles/11725453-set-up-the-claude-lti-in-canvas-by-instructure) and data/claude/claude-for-education/11139094-getting-started-with-claude-for-education-at-your-university-for-owners-admins.md.
"i am in US Virgin Islands and the merchant is saying i have to spend minimum 10$ on my VISA card, why so?",Visa card minimum spend,visa,"In the USA and US territories—including the US Virgin Islands, Puerto Rico, and Guam—merchants are permitted to establish a minimum transaction amount of up to US$10 for Visa credit card purchases. This is an exception to the general Visa rule that prohibits merchants from setting minimum or maximum transaction limits. Please note that this exception applies only to credit cards; merchants are not permitted to require a minimum purchase amount for Visa debit card transactions. If you are being asked for a minimum spend on a debit card, or if a merchant requires more than $10 for a credit card transaction, we recommend notifying your Visa card issuer (the bank that provided your card) to report the issue.",Merchant Rules,replied,product_issue,"According to data/visa/support.md, while merchants generally cannot set transaction limits, an exception in the USA and US territories (specifically naming the US Virgin Islands) allows a minimum transaction amount of US$10 for credit cards only. The same source states that users should notify their card issuer if merchants apply these limits to debit cards or exceed the $10 threshold."
